  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "A diagram titled 'DETERMINANT LAYERS OF UHC' showing horizontal coverage bars grouped by category (Cost: Financial coverage; Quality: Effective coverage; Demand: Continuous coverage, Contact coverage; Supply: Accessibility of health facilities, Availability of human resources, Availability of commodities and equipment; Accountability: Accountability coverage, Target population, Total population). Each of the top eight bars ends in a lettered circle (A-H) connected by a dotted line, representing the current performance gap, to a vertical red bar labelled 'TARGET: universal effective coverage of health interventions of known efficacy'. A side panel titled 'mHEALTH STRATEGIES' lists, for each letter, the mHealth applications that can close that gap: H - Mobile financial transactions; G - Decision support, POC diagnostics, Telemedicine, Reminders, Incentives; F - Persistent electronic health records, Provider-to-provider communication, Work planning, Reminders; E - Behavior change communication (BCC), Incentives; D - Hotlines, Client mobile apps, Client information content subscriptions; C - Human resource management, Provider training, Telemedicine; B - Supply management, Counterfeit prevention; A - Client registration, Electronic medical records, Unique identifiers, Data collection and reporting, Screening tools, Civil registration and vital events. A legend below explains the dotted line as the current gap in determinant performance, the circle-and-arrow as illustrative mHealth strategies to close performance gaps, and a dashed vertical line as the minimum performance of the supply determinant.",
      "state": "draft",
      "drafted_by": {
